🐛 Describe the bug
Some of the headers of the stable API have anonymous namespaces inside of them:



      pytorch/torch/csrc/stable/stableivalue_conversions.h


        Lines 11 to 13
      in
      264e7f6







           // use anonymous namespace to avoid collisions between differing 




           // versions of this file that may be included by different sources 




           namespace { 





This is considered an anti-pattern, and it has the side effect that the global to and from names are overloaded in every file that includes those headers.
I'm not sure whether I fully grasp the original reason for using an anonymous namespace, but I wonder whether an anonymous namespace inside a named namespace would work. Something like this:
namespace torch::stable {
namespace {
template <typename T>
StableIValue from(T val);
template <typename T>
T to(StableIValue val);
}
}
